It talks to the Slack Web API and to Slack Socket Mode
(https://docs.slack.dev) with the tokens of a Slack app that each user creates
in their own workspace. This integration is unofficial: it is not affiliated
with nor endorsed by Slack Technologies, LLC. Slack is a trademark of Slack
Technologies, LLC. No logo or brand mark of Slack is used: the cover is a
generic illustration.

It depends on:
  - @gladysassistant/integration-sdk (Apache License 2.0);
  - ws (https://github.com/websockets/ws, MIT License), already a dependency
    of the SDK, for the Socket Mode WebSocket (ping/pong).

Design inspiration, read only, no code copied:
  - the Socket Mode client of the official Slack SDK for Node.js
    (https://github.com/slackapi/node-slack-sdk, MIT License): the ping
    timeouts and the retry_attempt field of the envelopes;
  - the Mattermost, Rocket.Chat and Zulip integrations for Gladys by guim31
    (https://github.com/guim31): linking a chat account with a code sent to
    the bot, the age limit of re-delivered messages.

callemand/gladys-slack (2018) is a Gladys 3 module, unrelated to this
integration.
